Title:  ir3/array_to_ssa: don't resolve readers to deleted phis
Author: TobiasWienand
URL:    https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46182
Head:   347da075a10b3163e395223485808c17f0abf951 (MR state opened, target main, checked 21 Nov 2026)
Review: none (Job Noorman engaged, asked for a fossil; fossil posted 19 Nov)
Apply:  applies on staging/26.3 6cd33b7f68ee after the patches before it, without conflict or backport

From f1dcaedcbdc02f025109170320d093f5cabe37a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tobias <tobiaswienand11235@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:04:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ir3/array_to_ssa: don't resolve readers to deleted phis

remove_trivial_phi() breaks cycles by returning the dst of the phi it
is still visiting. A phi can therefore resolve to a phi that is found
trivial and deleted later. lookup_value() follows only one step, so
readers can keep a def that is no longer in the program. In the issue,
ir3_lower_shared_phis allocates a use set for that def and frees it,
and ir3_cf then adds to the freed set.

Follow the chain until it reaches a def that is not a deleted phi. Each
step moves to a phi that finished later, so the chain ends.

Add a test that builds such a CFG and checks that every source still
points at an instruction in the program.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/16629
Fixes: ca15116fa13 ("ir3/array_to_ssa: fix updating/removing phis")
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c   |   9 +-
 src/freedreno/ir3/meson.build          |  12 +++
 src/freedreno/ir3/tests/array_to_ssa.c | 131 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 148 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/freedreno/ir3/tests/array_to_ssa.c

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
index dacd516d30a..cb69f0d47ec 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_array_to_ssa.c
@@ -161,10 +161,11 @@ remove_trivial_phi(struct ir3_instruction *phi)
 static struct ir3_register *
 lookup_value(struct ir3_register *reg)
 {
-   if (!reg)
-      return NULL;
-   if (reg->instr->opc == OPC_META_PHI)
-      return reg->instr->data;
+   /* A removed phi can resolve to another phi that was removed later, so
+    * follow the chain until we reach a definition that is kept.
+    */
+   while (reg && reg->instr->opc == OPC_META_PHI && reg->instr->data != reg)
+      reg = reg->instr->data;
    return reg;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/meson.build b/src/freedreno/ir3/meson.build
index 962a53c7f2a..45906be9641 100644
